      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Monomials & Polynomials):</b> The formula <b>P(x) = a₄x⁴ + a₃x³ + a₂x² + a₁x + a₀</b> is spoken: <i>'Pee of ex equals ay-four ex to the fourth, plus ay-three ex cubed, plus ay-two ex squared, plus ay-one ex, plus ay-zero'</i>. It is a sum of 5 elementary power building blocks (monomials):<ul><li><b>a₀</b> <i>('ay-zero')</i> — constant vertical lift shifting the entire curve up or down;</li><li><b>a₁·x</b> <i>('ay-one ex')</i> — linear slope (tangent velocity at x = 0);</li><li><b>a₂·x²</b> <i>('ay-two ex squared')</i> — U-shaped parabolic bowl (curvature at x = 0);</li><li><b>a₃·x³</b> <i>('ay-three ex cubed')</i> — S-shaped cubic wave with an inflection point;</li><li><b>a₄·x⁴</b> <i>('ay-four ex to the fourth')</i> — double-bottom W-shaped quartic well.</li></ul><b>Dominance Law:</b> near zero (|x| &lt; 1) lower powers <b>a₀ + a₁x + a₂x²</b> shape the curve, whereas far from zero (|x| ≫ 1) the highest degree term <b>a₄x⁴</b> dominates everything!",
    w1_story_roots:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Factorization, Vieta's Formulas & the Fundamental Theorem of Algebra):</b> Every degree-<b>n</b> polynomial can be written as a product of root factors: <b>P(x) = a·(x − r₁)(x − r₂)(x − r₃)</b> <i>(spoken: 'Pee of ex equals ay times (ex minus ar-one)(ex minus ar-two)(ex minus ar-three)')</i>.<ul><li><b>Why roots zero out P(x):</b> plugging in <b>x = r₁</b> turns the first factor into zero <b>(r₁ − r₁ = 0)</b>, annihilating the entire product!</li><li><b>Vieta's Theorem:</b> expanding the brackets directly links the sum and products of the roots <b>rₖ</b> to the coefficients <b>aₖ</b>.</li><li><b>Gauss's Fundamental Theorem of Algebra:</b> a degree-<b>n</b> polynomial <i>always</i> has exactly <b>n</b> roots in the complex plane <b>ℂ</b> — when a curve lifts off the X-axis, pairs of real roots collide and rotate 90° into complex conjugate pairs <b>u ± i·v</b> on the ℂ Radar!</li></ul>",
    w1_story_taylor:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Taylor Series & Horner's Scheme):</b> A silicon CPU/GPU cannot directly compute transcendental waves like <b>sin(x)</b>, <b>cos(x)</b>, or <b>eˣ</b> — its ALU hardware only knows addition <b>(+)</b> and multiplication <b>(×)</b>!<ul><li><b>Taylor Series — Tₙ(x) = Σ [f⁽ᵏ⁾(0) / k!]·xᵏ</b> <i>(spoken: 'Tee-en of ex equals the sum of the kay-th derivative at zero divided by kay-factorial times ex to the kay')</i>: by matching a wave's height, velocity, acceleration, and higher derivatives at <b>x = 0</b>, a polynomial clones the wave with arbitrary precision!</li><li><b>Horner's Scheme — P(x) = (((a₄x + a₃)x + a₂)x + a₁)x + a₀</b> <i>(spoken: 'Horner nested brackets')</i>: factoring out <b>x</b> recursively cuts 10 multiplications down to just <b>4 hardware FMA (Fused Multiply-Add) cycles</b>!</li></ul>",
    w1_story_bezier:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Bézier Splines & Bernstein Basis vs Lagrange Interpolation):</b> How do we make a polynomial curve pass near or through control points <b>P₀..P₃</b>? Two mathematical paradigms compete:<ul><li><b>Bézier Curve — B(t) = Σ Pₖ · bₖ,ₙ(t)</b>, where <b>bₖ,ₙ(t) = Cₙᵏ · tᵏ · (1 − t)ⁿ⁻ᵏ</b> <i>(spoken: 'Bee of tee equals sum of control points Pee-kay times Bernstein basis polynomials bee-kay-en of tee')</i>: Bernstein weights are non-negative and sum to <b>1</b> for every <b>t ∈ [0, 1]</b> (partition of unity), trapping the curve smoothly inside the convex hull of its control magnets!</li><li><b>Lagrange Polynomial — L(x) = Σ yₖ · lₖ(x)</b> <i>(spoken: 'El of ex equals sum of heights why-kay times Lagrange basis el-kay of ex')</i>: forces a single high-degree polynomial through every point, triggering violent boundary oscillations known as <b>Runge's Phenomenon</b>!</li></ul>",
