    btn_reset_cam: "↺ 3D Camera",
    w2_story:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Analytical Modulus Landscape & Minimum Modulus Principle):</b> Replace real input <b>x</b> with a complex variable <b>z = x + i·y</b> <i>(spoken: 'zee equals ex plus eye why', where <b>x = Re(z)</b>, <b>y = Im(z)</b>, and <b>i² = −1</b> is a 90° rotation)</i>. Above every point of the complex floor <b>(x, iy)</b> we plot the modulus height <b>h(x,y) = |P(x + iy)| = √((Re P)² + (Im P)²) ≥ 0</b> <i>(spoken: 'aitch of ex,why equals modulus of Pee of ex plus eye why')</i>:<ul><li><b>Minimum Modulus Principle (Cauchy–Riemann):</b> an analytic complex function can never have a local minimum hanging in mid-air at <b>h &gt; 0</b> — every true valley bottom of <b>|P(z)|</b> must pierce all the way down to <b>h = 0</b>! That geometrically guarantees every polynomial has complex roots.</li><li><b>2D-to-3D Bridge:</b> the glowing yellow seam at <b>y = 0</b> is the exact vertical cross-section along the real X-axis (your 2D graph from Window #1).</li></ul>",
    w2_story_trampoline:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Analytical Modulus Landscape & Minimum Modulus Principle):</b> Replace real input <b>x</b> with a complex variable <b>z = x + i·y</b> <i>(spoken: 'zee equals ex plus eye why', where <b>x = Re(z)</b>, <b>y = Im(z)</b>, and <b>i² = −1</b> is a 90° rotation)</i>. Above every point of the complex floor <b>(x, iy)</b> we plot the modulus height <b>h(x,y) = |P(x + iy)| = √((Re P)² + (Im P)²) ≥ 0</b> <i>(spoken: 'aitch of ex,why equals modulus of Pee of ex plus eye why')</i>:<ul><li><b>Minimum Modulus Principle (Cauchy–Riemann):</b> an analytic complex function can never have a local minimum hanging in mid-air at <b>h &gt; 0</b> — every true valley bottom of <b>|P(z)|</b> must pierce all the way down to <b>h = 0</b>! That geometrically guarantees every polynomial has complex roots.</li><li><b>2D-to-3D Bridge:</b> the glowing yellow seam at <b>y = 0</b> is the exact vertical cross-section along the real X-axis (your 2D graph from Window #1).</li></ul>",
    w2_story_bezier3d:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Bicubic Tensor-Product Bézier Surface):</b> To generalize a 1D Bézier curve into a smooth 3D aerodynamic wing or car body panel, we multiply two Bernstein polynomial bases along longitudinal parameter <b>u ∈ [0, 1]</b> and spanwise parameter <b>v ∈ [0, 1]</b>: <b>S(u, v) = Σᵢ Σⱼ bᵢ,₃(u) · bⱼ,₃(v) · Pᵢⱼ</b> <i>(spoken: 'surface Es of you,vee equals double sum of Bernstein basis bee-eye of you times bee-jay of vee times control net Pee-eye-jay')</i>.<ul><li><b>Convex Hull & Continuity:</b> the 16 control points <b>Pᵢⱼ</b> form a 3D magnetic cage that distributes curvature smoothly across the patch without creases.</li><li><b>Where used:</b> the mathematical foundation of NURBS and Subdivision Surfaces in Maya, Houdini, Blender, and aerospace CAD.</li></ul>",
    badge_3d_info: "Floor: (x, iy) • Height: |P(x+iy)| ≥ 0 • Yellow Seam (y=0) = 2D Graph • Beacons = Roots",
    hint_3d_mouse: "Drag colored 3D points (roots / apex / wing) or drag empty space to orbit • Wheel — Zoom",
    w2_ctrl_title: "3D Relief & Cutting Plane Controls",
    w2_ctrl_desc:
      "When the <b>green Clutch LED light is ON</b>, this 3D trampoline is driven live by Window #1. Sweep <b>a₀ (height)</b> from negative to positive: watch the two green root funnels on the central seam race together, collide at (0,0), and split sideways as pink complex funnels along the <b>iY</b> axis!",
    sl_3d_c0: "a₀ — Bowl Lift",
    sl_3d_c2: "a₂ — x² Steepness",
    sl_3d_slice: "Depth Slice y₀",
    chk_slice: "Glowing 2D Slice (at y=0 this is the 2D world)",
