    w3_badge: "WINDOW #3 • 4D HYPERSPACE [WEBGL2]",
    w3_title: "4D Origami: Surface z₁ⁿ + z₂ⁿ = c, Hopf Fibration & Calabi–Yau",
    mp0: "Hopf Fibration (S³ → S²)",
    mp1: "Calabi–Yau Quintic (n = 5)",
    mp2: "Toroidal Root Knot",
    w3_story:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Complex Space ℂ² ≅ ℝ⁴ & the Hopf Fibration π: S³ → S²):</b> Two complex variables <b>z₁ = x₁ + i·y₁</b> and <b>z₂ = x₂ + i·y₂</b> span four-dimensional Euclidean space <b>ℂ² ≅ ℝ⁴</b> with four real axes <b>(x₁, y₁, x₂, y₂)</b> <i>(spoken: 'complex two-space see-two is isomorphic to real four-space ar-four')</i>. The unit equation <b>|z₁|² + |z₂|² = 1</b> defines the three-sphere <b>S³ ⊂ ℂ²</b> <i>(spoken: 'three-sphere es-three')</i>:<ul><li><b>Heinz Hopf's Theorem (1931) — π(z₁, z₂) = z₁ / z₂:</b> taking the ratio of the two complex coordinates fibers the entire 4D hypersphere <b>S³</b> into nested Clifford tori of closed circles, where every pair of distinct fibers is topologically linked like chainmail without intersecting!</li><li><b>SO(4) Double Rotation:</b> in 4D space, rotations act across <b>6 independent coordinate planes</b> simultaneously, turning the Clifford tori inside out through the central throat.</li></ul>",
    w3_story_p0:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Complex Space ℂ² ≅ ℝ⁴ & the Hopf Fibration π: S³ → S²):</b> Two complex variables <b>z₁ = x₁ + i·y₁</b> and <b>z₂ = x₂ + i·y₂</b> span four-dimensional Euclidean space <b>ℂ² ≅ ℝ⁴</b> with four real axes <b>(x₁, y₁, x₂, y₂)</b> <i>(spoken: 'complex two-space see-two is isomorphic to real four-space ar-four')</i>. The unit equation <b>|z₁|² + |z₂|² = 1</b> defines the three-sphere <b>S³ ⊂ ℂ²</b> <i>(spoken: 'three-sphere es-three')</i>:<ul><li><b>Heinz Hopf's Theorem (1931) — π(z₁, z₂) = z₁ / z₂:</b> taking the ratio of the two complex coordinates fibers the entire 4D hypersphere <b>S³</b> into nested Clifford tori of closed circles, where every pair of distinct fibers is topologically linked like chainmail without intersecting!</li><li><b>SO(4) Double Rotation:</b> in 4D space, rotations act across <b>6 independent coordinate planes</b> simultaneously, turning the Clifford tori inside out through the central throat.</li></ul>",
    w3_story_p1:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Fermat Algebraic Surface z₁ⁿ + z₂ⁿ = c & Calabi–Yau Quintic):</b> The complex polynomial equation <b>z₁ⁿ + z₂ⁿ − c = 0</b> <i>(spoken: 'zee-one to the en plus zee-two to the en minus see equals zero')</i> carves out a smooth Riemann hypersurface in <b>ℂ²</b> woven from <b>n</b> phase sheets <b>exp(2πi·k/n)</b>:<ul><li><b>Yau's Theorem (R_μν = 0, spoken: 'Ricci curvature tensor ar mew-new equals zero'):</b> at degree <b>n = 5</b> ('quintic'), the polynomial curvature cancels out across all complex directions, yielding a Ricci-flat Kähler metric that solves Einstein's vacuum field equations!</li><li><b>Superstring Compactification:</b> in 10-dimensional string theory, the 6 extra spatial dimensions are curled into microscopic Calabi–Yau manifolds whose topological holes govern particle physics.</li></ul>",
    w3_story_p2:
      "<b>Mathematical Essence (Algebraic Knots & Milnor Fibration z₁ᵖ + z₂ᵍ = 0 ∩ S³):</b> What happens when a singular complex polynomial curve <b>P(z₁, z₂) = z₁ᵖ + z₂ᵍ = 0</b> <i>(spoken: 'zee-one to the pee plus zee-two to the cue equals zero')</i> intersects a small 3-sphere <b>S³</b> surrounding the origin in <b>ℂ²</b>?<ul><li><b>John Milnor's Fibration Theorem:</b> the intersection of the polynomial zero locus with <b>S³</b> ties a closed <b>(p, q)-torus knot</b> in 3D space that winds <b>p</b> times around the meridian and <b>q</b> times around the longitude of a Clifford torus!</li><li><b>Algebra-to-Topology Bridge:</b> varying degree <b>n</b> and Clifford phase torsion <b>Ξ</b> directly alters the braiding and crossing number of the algebraic knot.</li></ul>",
