        b2: "<b>Where to look (3 key landmarks):</b><ol><li><b>Bright yellow neon seam down the middle (y = 0)</b> — literally your 2D school graph from Window #1! Click <b>'👁 Side View (2D Slice)'</b> to align the camera in profile and verify the exact match.</li><li><b>Sharp funnels & dashed laser beacons on the floor</b> — green (real) and pink (complex) roots of the polynomial.</li><li><b>Colored 3D spheres on the surface</b> — interactive 3D handles! Drag them directly in 3D space to lift the bowl, spread roots, or sculpt the 3D Bézier wing.</li></ol>",
        b3: "<b>Camera & Tab Controls:</b> Drag empty space with the left mouse button to orbit the 3D camera; scroll the wheel to zoom. Switch between <b>'1. 3D Trampoline'</b> and <b>'2. 3D Bézier Wing'</b> in the toolbar to update the mathematical explanation above the viewport."
