        b2: "<b>Resizable On-Screen HUD Instruments:</b><ul><li>Top-left: <b>'4D Rotation · SO(4)'</b> (spinor phase dial & degree <b>n</b>) and <b>'Poincaré Section · ∂Ω'</b> (live 2D cross-section tomograph).</li><li>Top-right: <b>'4D Shape Passport'</b> table with equations and topological invariants. <b>Every HUD card can be freely resized</b> by dragging its corner grip <b>↙ / ↘</b>!</li></ul>",
        b3: "<b>Mouse & Preset Controls:</b> Drag anywhere in space to orbit smoothly in 3D (scroll wheel to zoom). Click the 3 preset tabs at the top (<b>Hopf Fibration</b>, <b>Calabi–Yau Quintic</b>, <b>Toroidal Root Knot</b>) to switch both the 4D geometry and the mathematical lesson above the stage!"
